  "description": "B94: Common Lime -  2m Crown reduction, remove Deadwood.\r460: English Oak - Upper south-east primary branch has a fracture at 12m over roadway, Reduce defective branch to fracture point. Deadwood. 1-2m reduction of lower east primary branch.\r4493: Ash - Fell to 2m. (Dead)\r464: English Oak - Fell to 5m (Dead). \r1326: Hornbeam - Kretszchmaria fruiting bodies emerging from base to south. Is weighted to the south. - Pollard at 7m\r1371: English Oak - Pollard at 5m and retain as monolith. \r1150a: Sycamore - Numerous historic topping wounds at 6m decaying extensively\tReduce tree to 5m. \r1214a: Larch - North primary lateral excessively end-weighted over neighbouring garden\t2m reduction of north primary branch. Deadwood. \r1363: English Oak - Very large Ganoderma resinaceum at base to west. Wood tapped out very altered around it - the canopy is stagheading. No open cavity observed but more altered wood now. Reduce tree to 10m. \r4691: Evergreen Magnolia - Cavity probed to 450mm of 550mm tangentially into south-east stem. Decay gets worse into butt. 1-1.5m canopy reduction\r1969: Larch - Fell to 2m. (Dead). \r381: Common Lime - Remove Deadwood. Raise lower canopy up to 6m. \rB131: Holly - Fell to 2m. (Dead). \r4473: Turkey Oak - Remove Deadwood. Raise lower canopy up to 3m.\rB156: Robinia - North lower canopy weakly attached to stem. 1-1.5m canopy reduction of north canopy.\rB217: English Oak - Reduce down to 10m. (Dead). \r4029: Cedar of Lebanon - All primary branches becoming end-weighted again. One upper lateral lost to north-west 1.5m reduction of north and west canopy. \r574: Robinia - Gap in canopy between subject tree and adjacent one. Is on escarpment. Appears to be in slow collapse over road. Fell. \r",
